<title>BELGIUM: EU allocates preferential cane sugar import quota.</title>
<headline>EU allocates preferential cane sugar import quota.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union has allocated a 265,000 tonnes reduced tariff raw cane sugar import quota between Portugal, Finland and France, EU member state officials said on Friday.</p>
<p>The EU sugar management committee, which agreed the quota on Wednesday, allocated Portugal 205,000 tonnes, Finland 48,000 tonnes and France 12,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>The three countries received 162,000 tonnes, 50,000 tonnes and 10,000 tonnes respectively this season.</p>
<p>The sugar will be supplied by African, Caribbean and Pacific (ACP) countries and India at a reduced tariff of 5.41 Ecus per tonne between July 1 and February 28, 1998.</p>
<p>--Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
